  "question": {
    "text": "Let the area of the triangle with vertices <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;sq. units. If the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;are collinear, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math> is equal to"
  },
